# 3D Gallery: build contract

Product: an artist shows their work on a venue's own walls at true scale. Two roles: **P1 artist** (sets up, arrange mode) and **P2 venue owner** (views a link, must need zero learning).

When asked to **build FEAT-XX** (or any feature work in `app/`), follow [FEATURES.md § Build handoff contract](../../FEATURES.md#build-handoff-contract).

Short version:

1. Work on `feat/feat-XX-<name>` branched from up-to-date `main`, never on `main`.
2. Sources, in priority order on conflict: **behavior** → `features/FEAT-XX-*.md` (REQs, AC, flow map) then `FLOWS.md` shared rules; **look & a11y** → `docs/ux-principles.md` + `docs/ui-patterns.md`; **tech** → `PRD-3d-gallery.md` §6.1 + §7 + resolved decisions in `FEATURES.md`.
3. Build every flow-map node incl. loading, error, empty, and reduced-motion states.
4. Before finishing: `npm run lint`, `npm run typecheck`, `npm run build` pass in `app/`; give a click-through checklist mapped to AC.
5. Update FEAT status + `FEATURES.md` Changelog.

## Tech guardrails

- **True scale:** all sizes come from venue/artwork JSON in inches; convert to meters in one helper. Never resize art or walls to fit.
- **Restaurant hang height:** default vertical position comes from one shared `recommendedCenter` helper (keep-clear zone from `wainscotIn` / `furnitureTopIn` + `clearanceIn`, min 57 in center). See PRD § Hang height. Never hard-code 57 in.
- Content lives in `app/src/data/artworks.json` and `app/src/data/venues/<id>.json`, not in scene code.
- Owner-facing navigation is saved viewpoints + limited drag-to-look. Don't add free-walk/WASD controls.
- Arrange mode is dev-only (`npm run dev` + `?arrange`) and must never ship in production builds.
- Renderer: `THREE.WebGLRenderer` (Spark, used for scans, does not support `WebGPURenderer`) unless D-01 changes.
- Cloud-first: the dev laptop has integrated graphics. No local 3D processing; keep `low` quality as the dev default.
- Hosting: GitHub Pages from `main` (public repo, D-03). Vite `base: '/3d-gallery/'`; generate `v/<id>/index.html` per venue at build. Add `noindex`; never list venues on an index page; commit cropped wall photos only.
- Large assets (> 50 MB) are hosted outside git; see `docs/ASSET-PIPELINE.md`.
- Deploy only from `main`.

Don't commit or push unless asked.
